                <pb facs="0241" n="123" sameAs="frus:frus1929v03/pg123"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">314.115C43/22: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Minister in
                        Guatemala</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Geissler</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1928-05-19T16:00:00-04:00">May 19, 1928—4
                    p.m.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p>44. Department informed that Percy W. Shufeldt of Belize, British Honduras, has a
                    concession which he has been operating for some years for the exploitation of
                    chicle in Guatemala and that bill is now before Guatemalan Congress to cancel
                    the concession. Please investigate and report.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Kellogg</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
